  "title": "Prolon Almond and Cocoa Spread Recalled Nationwide After Undeclared Nut Allergens Discovered",
  "summary": "A popular almond and cocoa spread sold online across the United States has been recalled after testing found additional tree nut allergens that were not identified on the product label. The recall affects a specific lot of Prolon Apulian Almond & Cocoa Spread, according to L-Nutra and the U.S. Food and Drug Administration. The California-based company said the affected product may contain cashew, pistachio, and hazelnut, creating a potentially serious health risk for people who are allergic or",
